# escape_puca_ring -- the hall under the hill: a púca caught dancing in a fairy ring, and unable to stop
#
# PLACEHOLDERS: each card says what happens. The real words (and their Irish) to be written.
# Its last card sets escape_puca_ring_free: it goes, a horse of the air (it will turn up again, later in the game).

@file underworld/escape
@encounter 2

= node 0 — dancing
@when !note escape_puca_ring_free
@continue
[PLACEHOLDER] The púca dances in the ring and cannot stop. It laughs at itself, between breaths.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
It asks you to break the ring.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= node 1 — out
@when !note escape_puca_ring_free
@note escape_puca_ring_free
[PLACEHOLDER] You kick a toadstool out of the ring. The púca stops, and is a horse of the air, and is gone.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
It will remember you.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
